<h1>Plastic Raw Material Recovery – Corona Grival</h1>
<p class="lead">Industrial project focused on evaluating and planning the recovery of plastic raw materials at the Funza plant.</p>
</section>
<section class="page-shell detail-layout">
<div class="detail-copy">
<h2>Project overview</h2>
<p>During my internship at Organización Corona, I contributed to the development of the Plastic Raw Material Recovery project at the Funza plant. The work covered strategic planning, concept development, product and process engineering, and preparation for industrial implementation.</p>
<p>The objective was to evaluate the technical, financial and environmental feasibility of recovering plastic material and reintegrating it into the production process.</p>
<h2>Engineering activities</h2>
<ul class="clean-list">
<li><strong>Financial Evaluation:</strong> Built a financial model using the company's evaluation template, comparing the current and proposed scenarios over a ten-year projection. The analysis included NPV, IRR and payback period.</li>
<li><strong>Sensitivity Analysis:</strong> Evaluated scenarios involving production volume, exchange-rate variation, initial investment and raw-material cost.</li>
<li><strong>Process Characterization:</strong> Characterized the plastic recovery process to identify the required technologies and equipment.</li>
<li><strong>Technology Selection:</strong> Researched suppliers and compared equipment based on cost, delivery time, after-sales service, energy consumption and country of origin.</li>
<li><strong>Plant Layout:</strong> Developed a proposed equipment layout for the recovery process, considering equipment dimensions, circulation space and relationships between process areas.</li>
<li><strong>Environmental Evaluation:</strong> Used Corona's Triple Account methodology to compare environmental indicators before and after the proposed investment.</li>
<li><strong>Safety Planning:</strong> Prepared initial safety and occupational health planning maps, to be completed after the equipment was installed.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Project results</h2>
<p>The financial evaluation reported a payback period of 3.49 years, a five-year IRR of 17.7% and a plant-layout efficiency score of 9. The environmental assessment projected reductions in electricity consumption, greenhouse gas emissions, water consumption and noise, alongside increased reuse of industrial plastic material.</p>
<p>The project also strengthened my experience in industrial project management, plastic processing, manufacturing technology evaluation and cross-functional collaboration.</p>
